The error log indicates a test failure in `test_ppp_frame_receive`. The assertion `received_packets_len == 1` fails, meaning the test thread does not see the received packet after feeding data to the modem PPP layer.

The function `put_and_validate_wrapped_frame` uses `k_yield()` to wait for the PPP processing to complete. This is a potential race condition, as `k_yield()` only gives up the CPU to threads of equal or higher priority and does not guarantee that the work queue processing the PPP data will complete before the test thread resumes.

Other tests in the same file use `k_msleep()` to allow sufficient time for asynchronous operations. The fix is to replace the `k_yield()` with a short `k_msleep()` to ensure the PPP processing work has time to execute before the test asserts the result.

